     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Exposure limit per underlying currency
+
+If you trade multiple pairs that share the same underlying (base) currency - for example several BTC pairs, or a handful of pairs that are all leveraged bets on the same coin - a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at once. `max_currency_exposure` lets you cap this concentration risk.
+
+Set `max_currency_exposure` to a ratio (fraction of your tradable capital, see [Tradable balance](#tradable-balance)) that may be committed, in total, to all *currently open* trades sharing the same underlying currency. When opening (or increasing) a trade would push the combined stake for that currency above the configured share, the stake amount is reduced to whatever headroom remains; if none remains, the trade is not opened.
+
+```json
+"max_currency_exposure": 0.3,
+```
+
+With the setting above, no more than 30% of your tradable capital may ever be committed at once to BTC/USDT, BTC/USDC, BTCUP/USDT, or any other pair whose base currency is BTC - regardless of how many of those pairs are in your whitelist or open at the same time.
+
+This setting is disabled by default (unlimited exposure per currency), and applies identically to live/dry-run trading and backtesting.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
